## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
**Part A — Why This Company Can Compound:**  
AI demand → Broadcom’s AI ASICs (e.g., Tomahawk/StrataXGS) → Meta, Google, and VMware adopt → Broadcom gains market share in data centers → reinforces its position as a critical supplier.  

**Part B — Capex Cycle Risk:**  
- **Severity: MEDIUM**  
Broadcom is fab-lite, reliant on TSMC for manufacturing, which introduces supply chain risks. Its customer concentration in the data center market (e.g., Meta and Google) exposes it to capex cycles. While AI demand mitigates some risk, dependence on external foundries and a single end-market make it vulnerable.

